Subproblem: Model Selection and Training
Node: Select and Train Model
Expected outcome: Train a model that performs well on validation data.

Next, we will select a model to train on the processed training dataset. Given the nature of the task (multi-label classification), we will use a Random Forest classifier, which is robust and can handle multi-label outputs effectively. We will also perform cross-validation to ensure the model generalizes well.

The steps will include:
1. Splitting the processed training data into features and labels.
2. Training the Random Forest model.
3. Evaluating the model using cross-validation to assess its performance.
