     - Assumptions: Linearity, independence.
     - Pros: Fast and interpretable.
     - Cons: May underperform with complex relationships.
     - Computational Cost: Low.
  
  B) **Random Forest**: Handles non-linear relationships and interactions.
     - Assumptions: None.
     - Pros: Robust to overfitting.
